\b\fs40 \cf0 \
Airdrop
\b0\fs24 \
\
AquaTransport makes it possible to use Airdrop with modern Macs and iPhones! To use this feature, your computer must be running OS X 10.9 Mavericks, and your hardware must support Bluetooth LE and 5 Ghz Wi-Fi with active Monitor Mode. An ethertap driver, included with the AquaTransport installer by default, must also be present.\
\
You will be disconnected from Wi-Fi while AirDrop is in use.\

\b\fs40 \
Twitter / BlueSky
\b0\fs24 \
\
You can use AquaTransport to log into your BlueSky account as if it was a Twitter account!\
\
First, in BlueSky, go to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/settings/app-passwords"}}{\fldrslt Settings 
\f1 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Privacy and security 
\f1 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  App passwords}} 
\f1 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  and add a new app password.\
\
Then, on your Mac, log in with your full BlueSky handle as the username (e.g. @johnappleseed.bsky.social) and your previously-generated app password as the password.\
\
This will work in System Preferences as well as in the official Twitter app for Mac, version 2.1.1 or earlier. To be clear, you will be using the Twitter 
\i app
\i0  to log into and use your 
\i BlueSky
\i0  account.\
\
Thank you to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://preloading.dev/"}}{\fldrslt Preloading}} for making this possible by building and hosting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twb.preloading.dev/"}}{\fldrslt TwitterAPIBridge}}!
