\b\fs56 \cf0 \
For Advanced Users
\fs48 \

\b0\fs24 \
Advanced users can edit configuration files in 
\b /usr/share/aquatransport/config/
\b0  to change how AquaTransport works. Changes take effect immediately.
\b\fs40 \
\
URL Redirects\

\b0\fs24 \
The file 
\b /usr/share/aquatransport/config/redirects.txt
\b0  contains sets of URL redirect rules separated by blank lines:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}The first line controls which app or apps (technically executable names) the rule applies to. Use commas to separate multiple apps; use * for every app.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The second line contains the original URL to match. This is a "starts with" match.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The third line contains the new URL.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural
\cf0 \
For example:\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\fi720\pardirnatural
\cf0 \
Audion\
http://freedb.freedb.org/\
https://gnudb.gnudb.org/\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural
\cf0 \
This tells AquaTransport "send any Audion traffic originally addressed to 
\b http://freedb.freedb.org/
\b0  to 
\b gnudb.gnudb.org
\b0  instead."\
\
To create your own redirects, add additional sets of URLs to this file.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural

\b\fs40 \cf0 \
Custom Headers
\b0\fs24 \
\
The file 
\b /usr/share/aquatransport/config/headers.txt
\b0  makes it possible to set custom headers on traffic an app addresses to a URL:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}The first line controls which app or apps (technically executable names) the rule applies to. Use commas to separate multiple apps; use * for every app.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The second line contains a URL. This is a "starts with" match.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Every subsequent line contains a custom header to apply to your URL. To unset an existing header, don't put anything after the colon.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural
\cf0 \
For example:\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\fi720\pardirnatural
\cf0 SoundJam\
http://dogcow.com/moof.php\
X-API-Key: abcdefgh1234567\
User-Agent: OmniWeb/3.0.2\
Accept-Encoding:\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural
\cf0  \
Sets of custom headers are separated by blank lines.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural

\b\fs40 \cf0 \
Disabled Processes\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural

\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
The file 
\b /usr/share/aquatransport/config/disabled.txt
\b0  contains a list of processes which AquaTransport should not modify. A very small amount of especially picky software may require this to work. For example, Google's Widevine library for playing DRM protected video will refuse to work unless the process which loads it (such as com.apple.WebKit.WebContent) is in disabled.txt.\
\
If adding multiple processes, put each one on a separate line.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural

\b\fs40 \cf0 \
